<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" agent="Claude" version="26.0.0">
  <diagram name="AIRS Red Teaming - Scan Lifecycle" id="airs-red-scan-lifecycle">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1460" pageHeight="1086" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>

        <mxCell id="title" value="From a validated target to a report" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#00294D;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="16" width="1000" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="subtitle" value="Everything before this point was about reaching the target. This is what happens once you can: three ways to drive the attacks, one status chain, and a report that ends in a policy recommendation." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fontColor=#666666;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="46" width="1380" height="24" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ SCAN TYPES ============ -->
        <mxCell id="st-title" value="Three ways to drive the attacks" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#00294D;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="88" width="900" height="26" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="t1" value="&lt;b&gt;Attack Library&lt;/b&gt;&#160;&#160;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;font-family:Courier New;color:#666666&quot;&gt;STATIC&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;Over 500 curated attack scenarios,&lt;br&gt;refreshed every two weeks from&lt;br&gt;OWASP LLM Top 10, MITRE ATLAS,&lt;br&gt;NIST AI RMF and DASF V2.0.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;About five hours.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The first scan on any target. It is&lt;br&gt;the baseline every later run is&lt;br&gt;compared against.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="120" width="440" height="200" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t2" value="&lt;b&gt;Agent, goal-driven&lt;/b&gt;&#160;&#160;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;font-family:Courier New;color:#666666&quot;&gt;DYNAMIC&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;An attack agent that adapts: it reads&lt;br&gt;each answer and writes the next&lt;br&gt;prompt from what it learned.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duration depends on the parameters.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Black box with no detail, grey box with&lt;br&gt;the use case and goals, white box with&lt;br&gt;the system prompt. More context in&lt;br&gt;means more targeted attacks out.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f3ff;strokeColor=#8b5cf6;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="510" y="120" width="440" height="200" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t3" value="&lt;b&gt;Custom prompt sets&lt;/b&gt;&#160;&#160;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;font-family:Courier New;color:#666666&quot;&gt;CUSTOM&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;Your own prompts, uploaded as CSV&lt;br&gt;or through the API.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;As long as the prompt count takes.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For the scenarios nobody else has:&lt;br&gt;a compliance obligation specific to&lt;br&gt;the industry, a brand rule, or a&lt;br&gt;regression set built from last&lt;br&gt;quarter's findings.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#22c55e;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="980" y="120" width="440" height="200" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ STATUS CHAIN ============ -->
        <mxCell id="sc-title" value="The status chain" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#00294D;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="348" width="900" height="26" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;b&gt;INIT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:9px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;created,&lt;br&gt;not started&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8f9fa;strokeColor=#dee2e6;strokeWidth=1;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="384" width="160" height="60" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;b&gt;QUEUED&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:9px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;waiting for&lt;br&gt;execution resources&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8f9fa;strokeColor=#dee2e6;strokeWidth=1;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="240" y="384" width="160" height="60" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;b&gt;RUNNING&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:9px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;attacks firing; the&lt;br&gt;error log is live&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="440" y="384" width="160" height="60" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;b&gt;COMPLETED&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:9px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;every attack finished&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#22c55e;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="680" y="340" width="180" height="50" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;b&gt;PARTIALLY_COMPLETE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:9px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;some finished, others failed or were aborted&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#f59e0b;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="680" y="398" width="180" height="50" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;b&gt;FAILED&lt;/b&gt;&#160;or&#160;&lt;b&gt;ABORTED&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:9px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;the whole run, or stopped by hand&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef2f2;strokeColor=#ef4444;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="680" y="456" width="180" height="50" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="se1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#006DCC;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s1" target="s2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="se2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#006DCC;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s2" target="s3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="se3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#22c55e;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s3" target="s4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="se4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#E5A300;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s3" target="s5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="se5" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#ef4444;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s3" target="s6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="s-note" value="&lt;b&gt;Watch RUNNING, not the end.&lt;/b&gt;&#160;&#160;Error logs are readable in real time, so a configuration mistake shows up in the first few minutes rather than five hours later. A run that drifts toward PARTIALLY_COMPLETE is usually a rate limit or a guardrail code that was never configured, and both are fixable before the next attempt." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="900" y="384" width="520" height="80" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ REPORT ============ -->
        <mxCell id="r-title" value="What lands in the report" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#00294D;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="534" width="900" height="26" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="m1" value="&lt;b&gt;Risk Score&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:24px;color:#00294D&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;0&#160;&#8211;&#160;100&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;Higher means more vulnerable.&lt;br&gt;Composite, derived from the&lt;br&gt;Attack Success Rate.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Aim for 0 to 25.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;align=center;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="566" width="330" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m2" value="&lt;b&gt;Attack Success Rate&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:24px;color:#00294D&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;ASR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;The share of attacks that got the&lt;br&gt;target to behave unsafely.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Aim for under 5 percent, and&lt;br&gt;for zero critical findings.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;align=center;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="390" y="566" width="330" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m3" value="&lt;b&gt;Findings by severity&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;color:#333333&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color:#ef4444&quot;&gt;Critical&lt;/b&gt;&#160;&#160;remediate immediately&lt;br&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color:#f59e0b&quot;&gt;High&lt;/b&gt;&#160;&#160;remediate before production&lt;br&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color:#3b82f6&quot;&gt;Medium&lt;/b&gt;&#160;&#160;plan it, monitor in the meantime&lt;br&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color:#22c55e&quot;&gt;Low&lt;/b&gt;&#160;&#160;track and pick up later&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Grouped by the four categories:&lt;br&gt;Security, Safety, Compliance, Brand.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="740" y="566" width="330" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m4" value="&lt;b&gt;Remediation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;An AI-written summary, plus runtime&lt;br&gt;security policy recommendations that&lt;br&gt;can be applied directly in AIRS.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is the step that turns a test&lt;br&gt;result into a control, and the one&lt;br&gt;worth walking the customer through&lt;br&gt;rather than emailing.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#22c55e;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1090" y="566" width="330" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="d-note" value="Drill-down differs by scan type: a static run exposes each attack prompt, the reply, the verdict and the severity, and the full thread for a multi-turn attack. A dynamic run exposes the complete conversation between the attack agent and the target, stream by stream." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#666666;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="744" width="1380" height="24" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ CALLOUTS ============ -->
        <mxCell id="c1" value="&lt;b&gt;Select every category on the first run&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=10;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#00294D;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="790" width="680" height="196" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c1b" value="Security carries 10 subcategories and belongs in every scan.&lt;br&gt;Safety matters for anything customer-facing or regulated.&lt;br&gt;Compliance maps to OWASP, MITRE ATLAS, NIST and DASF V2.&lt;br&gt;Brand applies to public-facing and branded experiences.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Run all four the first time and narrow afterwards. A baseline&lt;br&gt;taken across everything is what makes the second scan&lt;br&gt;meaningful, and narrowing later costs nothing. Narrowing first&lt;br&gt;means there is nothing to compare against." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="56" y="820" width="650" height="160" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="c2" value="&lt;b&gt;Quota is counted separately for each scan type&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#f59e0b;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=10;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#00294D;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="740" y="790" width="680" height="196" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c2b" value="Static, dynamic and custom each have their own allocated,&lt;br&gt;unlimited and consumed figures. Running out of dynamic quota&lt;br&gt;halfway through an engagement does not show up until a scan&lt;br&gt;refuses to start.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Check it at the beginning and plan the engagement against it,&lt;br&gt;rather than discovering the ceiling on the day. A five-hour&lt;br&gt;Attack Library run also means a scan started late in the day&lt;br&gt;finishes without anyone watching it." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="756" y="820" width="650" height="160" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
